    narr:generatedFrom "7197e2e5261482e8ab862a8aa0f16ad8ffe0fb2f" ;
    narr:narration """A migration-programme call opens with [Tanya raising a never-before-opened question from legal about what happens to records left behind](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_1), and [Xavier asking which question](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_2). [Tanya frames the problem: open work migrates, eleven years of closed history does not](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_3), and [Xavier notes the vendor contract ends at last-site go-live](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_4). [A colleague admits assuming they'd keep paying the vendor to leave it running](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_6), which [Xavier calls the expensive, fragile answer](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_7). [His firm view: no read-only legacy platform — extract the closed history into a flat, self-describing archive](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_9), [defined as readable in ten years with nothing but the files](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_11), [because the data is easy to keep and the meaning is what rots](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_13). [Tanya adds her own argument: a live legacy platform invites dual systems of record](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_16), [which Xavier concedes is the better argument — decay versus behaviour](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_17), and [both go in the note](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_18). [Retention: legal's seven years from record date, with a longer claims-relevant hold to be set by legal in writing](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_20). [Tanya states the position — platform off at last go-live, extraction first, retention in writing before signing decommissioning terms](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_22), [Xavier signs up](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_23), [and the colleague insists it belongs in the vendor exit conversation, not after](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_24). [Tanya admits she'd have signed first and discovered the requirement afterwards](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_25), [rejects the usual order](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_27), and [Xavier commits to scoping by end of next week](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_28).""" ;
